%% title: Journal Posting Flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant TxSvc as transaction-service
    participant LedgerAPI as ledger-service\n(REST API)
    participant Domain as JournalDomain
    participant DB as PostgreSQL\n(partitioned journal)
    participant Outbox as outbox table
    participant Kafka as Kafka\nopenbank.ledger.journal.posted
    participant BalanceSvc as balance-service
    participant AuditSvc as audit-service

    TxSvc->>LedgerAPI: POST /api/v1/journals\n{transactionId, entryDate, valueDate, lines[]}
    LedgerAPI->>Domain: PostJournalCommand

    Domain->>Domain: validate per-currency balance\n(sum debits = sum credits per CCY)
    Domain->>Domain: check idempotency key\n(transactionId already posted?)

    Domain->>DB: BEGIN
    Domain->>DB: INSERT journal_entries\n(status=PENDING)
    Domain->>DB: INSERT journal_lines\n(D/C legs, amounts, fx_rate)
    Domain->>DB: UPDATE journal_entries\nSET status='POSTED'
    Domain->>Outbox: INSERT JournalPosted event
    Domain->>DB: COMMIT

    LedgerAPI-->>TxSvc: 201 Created {journalId, entryNumber}

    Note over Outbox,Kafka: Transactional outbox relay (async)
    Outbox->>Kafka: JournalPosted {journalId, transactionId,\nentryDate, lines[]}

    Kafka-->>BalanceSvc: update booked/available balance\n(ledger projection)
    Kafka-->>AuditSvc: append tamper-evident audit record

    Note over TxSvc,LedgerAPI: Reversal path
    TxSvc->>LedgerAPI: POST /api/v1/journals/{journalId}/reverse
    LedgerAPI->>DB: INSERT mirror journal_entry\n(status=POSTED, negated lines)
    LedgerAPI->>DB: UPDATE original SET status='REVERSED'
    LedgerAPI->>Outbox: INSERT JournalReversed event
    Outbox->>Kafka: JournalReversed {originalId, reversalId}
